From 678421be0c4ecd45f987cc0c7669499da1fd20ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 12:13:05 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: kodiak: switch the GIC to 4 interrupt cells

The Cortex-A55 and Cortex-A78 PMUs share PPI 7. Telling Linux which
CPUs each PMU serves takes a PPI partition phandle in a fourth interrupt
cell, which the GICv3 binding allows only with #interrupt-cells = <4>.

Switch the GIC to four cells and append 0 (no partition) to every GIC
interrupt specifier, in kodiak.dtsi and in the board files that route
the UART7 interrupt to the GIC. No functional change: the decoded
interrupts of all DTBs built from kodiak.dtsi are the same before and
after, apart from the added zero cell.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
